## SEVERITY / VERDICT
*Blocker:* a path beyond the one, numstat not `2 2`, a changed line other than the two, a removed or added line not matching the regexes, any `if:` or switch change, any other action or `with:`/`permissions` change, a pin that is not the commit `v2` resolves to, a tag-object sha, a sha not on Azure/login, a parse failure, a structural difference, a `Deploy demo` run caused by the PR, a NEW CodeQL alert at high+ or rule severity `error` or a `CodeQL` check-run concluded failure, a merge conflict or a merge tree other than main plus the one file, a gitleaks finding, a person name, decision-card id or secret in a message, or the head moved. *Major:* a builder claim contradicted that changes the basis (a blob, a count); no PRIOR WORK section; `Build` red at the head for a reason not shown to be a base fact; a collision with a live branch. *Minor/Note:* the ` # v2` comment names a moving tag; no master ancestry (release branch by design); unsigned commit; the builder's two slips; node differing from CI; the `mergeable_state` text. **GO** needs every check-run at the head completed and green (the neutral `CodeQL` replaced by a completed conclusion), all three Analyze runs complete with both thresholds met, `Build` completed green (the B4 rule applies), Checks 1-5, 7 clean and measured. While `build` or an Analyze run is pending the verdict is at most GO WITH FINDINGS and the line above the last line names the pending set. A NO GO sends a fix to a new builder seat with the fix-shape in prose and a ONE-line question only if a ruling is needed (a request to pin `actions/checkout` or to touch the switch is outside the ruling: a Note for Tuesday, never a defect). **STOP (`STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <the change and why>`)** if the delta holds a path beyond the one, a secret, a request that leaves loopback (other than GitHub GETs, the npm registry as `npm ci` reaches it), a premise moved (Check 2), or a security-shaped finding you cannot classify. **No escalation upward: you are tier 1.**
**First line of STATUS (the verdict line; at Step 0 the placeholder `GATE VERDICT B662: PENDING`):** `GATE VERDICT B662: pr113 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> @ 57784e7 (round 1 of 2 - delta <1 commit, 1 path, +2 -2, numstat 2 2 y/n; removed/added lines exact y/n; other paths byte-equal y/n> - conditions <only two uses lines y/n; if tests and switch untouched y/n; variables n, demo environment absent y/n, last 10 runs skipped y/n> - pin <v2 and v2.3.1 equal y/n; commit not tag object y/n; on Azure/login via <branch/release> y/n; tag re-read at verdict equal y/n> - structure <parse 6 of 6; EQUAL y/n; controls n of n DIFFERENT; rule RED(2) at main, CLEAN at head y/n> - deploy <Deploy demo runs for head n; trigger has no pull_request y/n> - CI <n completed success of n; pending <names|none>; failing <names|none>> - CodeQL <analyses n of 3 at the head; Analyze complete y/n; open alerts on PR ref n; new high+ n; new error n; #4 #5 instances on PR ref n; check-run conclusion x> - merge <ahead 1 behind 0 y/n; merge-tree clean y/n and equals GitHub's tree y/n; intersection empty y/n; main sha7 start and end> - jest <rd327 n tests equal y/n or NOT TESTED> - gitleaks rc <n>)`. Then sections: Step 0, REFUSE counts, PINS (start and verdict), instrument and load, Checks 1-8 each with the FAIL clock and evidence path, the pin-read table (both times), the mutant matrix, the run table, findings `B662-n` (severity, `path:line`, instrument, evidence class MEASURED AT RUNTIME / PROBED / READ ONLY; "none" is valid), the builder-claims table, FOR TUESDAY (the verdict in plain words; whether a forward merge is needed (expected no); what stands between the PR and a landing; after the landing read alerts #4 and #5 BY NUMBER on main's push analysis (must read `fixed`, any open is a STOP with the run id, never a dismissal), the `Deploy demo` run expected `skipped`, and the standing watch that the switch stays unset until a demo environment with a reviewer exists), FOUND / TESTED / HOW / NOT TESTED (at least: the pinned action in a real OIDC login; CodeQL closure of #4/#5; the Linux runner; `actionlint`) / corrections / processes, ports and trees left / **UNMEASURED**. **Last line, exactly one of:** `VERDICT: B662 pr113 b658/nexusai-815-pin-azure-login @ <sha7> <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> (round 1 of 2) on main <sha7>` (main by `ls-remote` at verdict; the line carries none of the words that name a landing; finding ids with severities and the CI state sit on the line above, e.g. `B662-1 Note, B662-2 Note; CI pending: build`), or `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>`.

**STATUS-NOW (binding).** Write `/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/!CODING/Datasec/NexusAI/1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-10-25_B662_STATUS.md` at Step 0 and update it after every check; evidence in `Briefs/2026-10-25_B662_evidence/` (summaries, hashes, TSVs; no secrets); your tools and logs in `session-tools/b662/` (with `_quarantine`, `logs`, `mut`); your clone `worktrees/b662-merge`. Do NOT write a `VERDICT:`, `STOPPED:` or `READY` line at the start of any line until you mean it: Tuesday's watcher reads only the file's last line. The LAST LINE while you work is `WORKING: <check and what is running, with a figure that moves>`. Heartbeat: every waiter and long job prints a moving figure (load1, `i of N`, elapsed seconds, log size) at least every 30 s into `session-tools/b662/logs/heartbeat.txt`; a figure unmoved for 3 beats means stuck: say so. Wait on a recorded pid (`kill -0`) or a done-marker file, never `pgrep -f` from a shell whose own argv holds the pattern. RESUME at about 80 percent of context: `WORKING: RESUME NEEDED at Check <n>` plus a RESUME section. A verdict from a gate that did not finish Checks 1, 3, 4 and 6 is conditional at best (add ` (conditional: <reason>)` to the first and last line).

